    <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 20pt;">Research Funding Rises Nearly 50% in a Single Year</h2>
      <p style="font-size: 11pt;">Loyola researchers overcame the budget-ary cutbacks that are plaguing many fund-ing agencies, securing significantly more research funding last year than the prev-ious year.</p>
      <p style="font-size: 11pt;">For the fiscal year ending June 30, 2008, lakeside campuses' faculty garnered a total of ${{ total_funding_amount }} in external support for research, a 40% increase over the amount received during FY 2007 (a ${{ previous_year_amount }} total external funding, en-compassing research, training, and infra-structure support, declined from ${{ previous_year_total }} to ${{ current_year_total }} during the same period, mainly because of fluctuations in amounts received for certain campus construction projects. The number of research awards also increased, from 52 to 56.</p>
