    <h2 style="font-size: 20pt;">New Internal Awards Stimulate Student and Faculty Research</h2>
    <p style="font-size: 11pt;">Associate Provost for Research Samuel Attoh recently announced two new inter-nal award programs. These are in keep-ing with his emphasis on using internal grant funds to leverage external funding to the maximum extent.</p>
    <p style="font-size: 11pt;">The first new program is the Research Incentive Award for Graduate Students (RIAG), which should $100 will be given to any Loyola graduate student on the lakeside campuses who submits a pro-posal for external funding to a Federal or private agency, as well as a bonus award of $1000 for any approved proposal.</p>
    <p style="font-size: 11pt;">The second new program is aimed at stimulating multidisciplinary research and building stronger partnerships with other</p>
    <div style="clear: both;"></div>
    <h3 style="font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 25px;">News from Federal Agencies</h3>
    <p style="font-size: 11pt;">The National Institutes of Health has issued a notice (NOT-OD-09-002) re-garding the Continuing Resolution signed by President Bush at the end of Septem-ber. As in the past when CRES have used, NIH will make non-competing re-search grant awards at a level below that indicated on the most recent Notice of Award (generally up to 90% of the previ-ously committed level).</p>
    <p style="font-size: 11pt;">Notice number NOT-OD-09-003 issued on October 8, 2008, states that "Beginning with original new applications (i.e., never submitted) and competing renewal applications submitted for the January 25, 2009 due dates and beyond, the NIH will accept only a single amend-</p>
    <p style="font-size: 11pt;">organizations and institutions. This year, two awards at a maximum level of ${{ award_amount_1 }} per project will be allocated to research teams that are prepared to sub-mit a multidisciplinary proposal to a na-tionally competitive funding agency. This support is intended to provide a basis for project development and pilot research, ultimately leading to independent fund-ing. The deadline for this year's competi-tion is December 5, 2008.</p>
    <p style="font-size: 11pt;">For additional information on all internal funding programs, please see http://www.luc.edu/ors/internalfunding.shtml.</p>
